{"event":"A forklift punctured a drum of liquid floor-stripper concentrate in a university teaching hospital's basement supply store, releasing a chemical spill that forced a partial evacuation of the laundry and linen level.","sources":["Imogen Harstad, linen services supervisor","Tovane University Hospital Facilities Log","Basement Level 2 Vapor Monitor","Desmond Okafor, forklift operator","Tovane Hospital Safety Office Incident Report"],"core":{"text":"At about 2:15 p.m. on a Thursday in early October, a drum of floor-stripper concentrate was punctured in the basement supply store of Tovane University Hospital and began leaking onto the concrete floor.","source":"Tovane University Hospital Facilities Log"},"facts":[{"text":"Desmond Okafor was moving a pallet of four 55-gallon drums from the loading bay to a storage rack when the incident occurred.","source":"Desmond Okafor, forklift operator"},{"text":"The leaking drum held an alkaline stripper containing ethanolamine, and about 30 gallons escaped before the drum was upended and sealed.","source":"Tovane Hospital Safety Office Incident Report"},{"text":"The Basement Level 2 Vapor Monitor registered an amine reading of 14 parts per million at 2:19 p.m.","source":"Basement Level 2 Vapor Monitor"},{"text":"The monitor's alarm threshold is set at 10 parts per million, and it sounded a local horn on the laundry level.","source":"Basement Level 2 Vapor Monitor"},{"text":"Imogen Harstad noticed a sharp, fishy smell drifting through the linen sorting room shortly before the horn sounded.","source":"Imogen Harstad, linen services supervisor"},{"text":"Harstad told her sorting crew to leave through the east stairwell and close the fire door behind them.","source":"Imogen Harstad, linen services supervisor"},{"text":"The Facilities Log records that the ventilation unit serving the supply store was switched to full exhaust at 2:24 p.m.","source":"Tovane University Hospital Facilities Log"},{"text":"A two-person hospital spill team in chemical suits began absorbing the liquid with granular pads at 2:41 p.m.","source":"Tovane Hospital Safety Office Incident Report"},{"text":"Okafor reported that a loose wooden pallet board had stuck out about six inches beyond the stack.","source":"Desmond Okafor, forklift operator"},{"text":"The pallet had been delivered that morning by an outside supplier and had not been rewrapped.","source":"Tovane Hospital Safety Office Incident Report"},{"text":"The vapor monitor readings fell below 10 parts per million at 3:32 p.m.","source":"Basement Level 2 Vapor Monitor"},{"text":"Clean linen deliveries to the surgical wing were delayed while the laundry level stayed closed.","source":"Imogen Harstad, linen services supervisor"},{"text":"The Facilities Log notes that the floor drain in the supply store was plugged with a rubber mat before the spill reached it.","source":"Tovane University Hospital Facilities Log"},{"text":"No patient areas were affected, and the Safety Office sent no one to the emergency department from the incident.","source":"Tovane Hospital Safety Office Incident Report"},{"text":"The contaminated absorbent was sealed into six lined containers for removal by a licensed waste contractor.","source":"Tovane Hospital Safety Office Incident Report"}],"disputes":[{"kind":"duration","about":"how long the laundry level stayed closed","claims":[{"text":"The laundry level stayed closed for about 90 minutes before staff were allowed back.","source":"Tovane University Hospital Facilities Log"},{"text":"The laundry level stayed closed for about 3 hours before staff were allowed back.","source":"Imogen Harstad, linen services supervisor"}]},{"kind":"cause","about":"what caused the drum to be punctured","claims":[{"text":"The sole cause of the puncture was the protruding pallet board striking the drum as the stack was lifted.","source":"Tovane Hospital Safety Office Incident Report"},{"text":"The sole cause of the puncture was a forklift fork tine being driven into the drum when the stack was set down.","source":"Desmond Okafor, forklift operator"}]}],"names":["Tovane University Hospital","Basement Level 2 Vapor Monitor","Tovane University Hospital Facilities Log","Tovane Hospital Safety Office Incident Report"]}

