Option: reassign the claim to a source that could know it. The Drive Controller Event Record could document a power supply fault, but it already records the trips and temperature, and assigning it there would be a plausible fix. However, the claim says "no jam contributed," which a controller record might not establish. Rewording is the safer route: keep Ostrowe as the source but make the claim about what he could observe, while keeping it incompatible with Thackeray's claim.

Thackeray's claim: the jam was the sole cause, nothing else contributed. Ostrowe could observe radio traffic and bags at the apron, but not the cause of the trips. A reworded claim that he could observe: "No bags were jammed on the feed conveyors from the apron side, so a jam was not the cause." Yet that still requires knowledge of the hall. Alternatively, reassigning to the Drive Controller Event Record is cleaner: "A fault in the shared drive power supply was the sole cause of the trips, and no jam contributed." A drive controller record plausibly documents power-supply faults and could record the absence of a jam-related overload. The same source is already used for the core, so this keeps balance, and the source list is unchanged. I'll reassign.

{"event":"A baggage reclaim carousel system at a small regional airport jammed and shut down during an evening arrivals bank, leaving passengers from several flights without their luggage for hours.","sources":["Terminal duty manager Imogen Thackeray","Hollowmere Regional Airport Baggage Control Log","Reclaim Hall Drive Controller Event Record","Ground handler Pavel Ostrowe","Hollowmere Airport Passenger Services Desk Tally"],"core":{"text":"The reclaim carousels in the arrivals hall of Hollowmere Regional Airport stopped moving during the evening arrivals bank on a Friday, shortly after 19:10.","source":"Reclaim Hall Drive Controller Event Record"},"facts":[{"text":"The drive controller recorded a fault trip on the Carousel 2 feed conveyor at 19:12, followed by trips on Carousels 1 and 3 within the next four minutes.","source":"Reclaim Hall Drive Controller Event Record"},{"text":"Three flights had landed in the preceding twenty-five minutes, and their bags were loaded onto the feed conveyors from the Tollbrook Apron baggage cart bay.","source":"Hollowmere Regional Airport Baggage Control Log"},{"text":"Pavel Ostrowe was driving a tug with four loaded carts toward the Tollbrook Apron bay when radio traffic told handlers to hold bags at the cart bay.","source":"Ground handler Pavel Ostrowe"},{"text":"Imogen Thackeray ordered the reclaim hall doors to the apron corridor closed to passengers at about 19:20 so that staff could clear the area.","source":"Terminal duty manager Imogen Thackeray"},{"text":"The Baggage Control Log lists a maintenance call to Wenlock Conveyor Services logged at 19:25.","source":"Hollowmere Regional Airport Baggage Control Log"},{"text":"Wenlock Conveyor Services technicians arrived in the reclaim hall after the call and began inspecting the carousel drive cabinets.","source":"Terminal duty manager Imogen Thackeray"},{"text":"The drive controller's temperature channel showed the Carousel 2 motor housing at 71 degrees Celsius when it tripped.","source":"Reclaim Hall Drive Controller Event Record"},{"text":"The Passenger Services Desk handed out written bag-delay forms to passengers from all three flights.","source":"Hollowmere Airport Passenger Services Desk Tally"},{"text":"Passenger Services staff set out water and seating along the far wall of the arrivals hall for waiting passengers.","source":"Terminal duty manager Imogen Thackeray"},{"text":"Handlers stacked the held bags on carts in rows inside the Tollbrook Apron bay, according to Pavel Ostrowe.","source":"Ground handler Pavel Ostrowe"},{"text":"The drive controller logged Carousels 1 and 3 restarted at 21:05 and Carousel 2 at 21:40.","source":"Reclaim Hall Drive Controller Event Record"},{"text":"The Baggage Control Log notes that a fourth flight, due at 20:30, was redirected to use the oversize belt for its reclaim.","source":"Hollowmere Regional Airport Baggage Control Log"},{"text":"Passenger Services recorded 214 completed delay forms by closing time.","source":"Hollowmere Airport Passenger Services Desk Tally"},{"text":"Thackeray remembers the hall smelling of warm rubber when she walked past Carousel 2.","source":"Terminal duty manager Imogen Thackeray"},{"text":"Ostrowe unloaded his last cart at the hall's side door and was told to keep the tug in the bay until released.","source":"Ground handler Pavel Ostrowe"}],"disputes":[{"kind":"cause","about":"sole cause of the carousel trips","claims":[{"text":"A jammed bag strap on the Carousel 2 feed conveyor was the sole cause of the trips, and nothing else contributed.","source":"Terminal duty manager Imogen Thackeray"},{"text":"A fault in the shared drive power supply was the sole cause of the trips, and no jam contributed.","source":"Reclaim Hall Drive Controller Event Record"}]},{"kind":"time","about":"time the first bags were returned to passengers after the restart","claims":[{"text":"The first bags reached passengers at 21:15 after the restart.","source":"Hollowmere Regional Airport Baggage Control Log"},{"text":"The first bags reached passengers at 21:30 after the restart.","source":"Hollowmere Airport Passenger Services Desk Tally"}]}],"names":["Hollowmere Regional Airport","Hollowmere Regional Airport Baggage Control Log","Hollowmere Airport Passenger Services Desk Tally","Tollbrook Apron","Wenlock Conveyor Services","Reclaim Hall Drive Controller Event Record"]}

{"event":"A fault in the hold-baggage screening conveyor at Tessarine Bay Airport halted the screening of checked bags during the midday departure bank on a Sunday, delaying baggage loading for several flights.","sources":["Tessarine Bay Airport Screening Hall Supervisor Odalys Merrin's statement","Tessarine Bay Airport Baggage Control Room Log","Screening Line 3 Drive Controller Event Record","Marlen Ground Handling Ramp Dispatch Sheet","Tessarine Bay Airport Security Operations Desk Log"],"core":{"text":"Screening Line 3, the hold-baggage x-ray conveyor at Tessarine Bay Airport, stopped at 11:26 on a Sunday and did not return to normal throughput until mid-afternoon.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Baggage Control Room Log"},"facts":[{"text":"The Screening Line 3 Drive Controller Event Record logged a motor overcurrent trip on the entry belt at 11:26:09.","source":"Screening Line 3 Drive Controller Event Record"},{"text":"Supervisor Odalys Merrin said she heard the belt grind down and saw about a dozen bags stacked at the x-ray tunnel mouth.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Screening Hall Supervisor Odalys Merrin's statement"},{"text":"The Baggage Control Room Log noted that Screening Lines 1 and 2 stayed in service throughout the stoppage.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Baggage Control Room Log"},{"text":"Bags from check-in desks 40 to 62 were redirected to Line 2, which has lower capacity than Line 3.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Baggage Control Room Log"},{"text":"The Screening Line 3 Drive Controller Event Record shows the drive tripped again at 12:03.","source":"Screening Line 3 Drive Controller Event Record"},{"text":"The Marlen Ground Handling Ramp Dispatch Sheet lists four departures with baggage loading started later than planned that afternoon.","source":"Marlen Ground Handling Ramp Dispatch Sheet"},{"text":"Marlen Ground Handling placed two extra loaders at the screened-bag chute to move bags faster once screening resumed.","source":"Marlen Ground Handling Ramp Dispatch Sheet"},{"text":"The Security Operations Desk Log records that a manual re-screening procedure was requested for bags flagged by the x-ray software before the stop.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Security Operations Desk Log"},{"text":"The Security Operations Desk Log shows a maintenance electrician was called to the screening hall at 11:34.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Security Operations Desk Log"},{"text":"Merrin said the electrician opened the drive cabinet beside the entry belt and the cabinet smelled warm.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Screening Hall Supervisor Odalys Merrin's statement"},{"text":"The Drive Controller Event Record shows motor current on the entry belt reading 31 amps at the first trip against a rated 24 amps.","source":"Screening Line 3 Drive Controller Event Record"},{"text":"The Baggage Control Room Log records Line 3 was cleared for normal throughput at 14:40.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Baggage Control Room Log"},{"text":"Merrin said passengers were asked to stay near check-in until their bag status was confirmed on two delayed flights.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Screening Hall Supervisor Odalys Merrin's statement"},{"text":"The Ramp Dispatch Sheet shows the final affected flight of the bank pushed back at 15:12.","source":"Marlen Ground Handling Ramp Dispatch Sheet"},{"text":"The Security Operations Desk Log notes that the screening hall was closed to non-staff from 11:40 until the line was cleared.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Security Operations Desk Log"}],"disputes":[{"kind":"duration","about":"how long Line 3 was fully out of service before partial throughput resumed","claims":[{"text":"The drive controller recorded Line 3 as stopped for about 75 minutes, from the first trip until bags could move again.","source":"Screening Line 3 Drive Controller Event Record"},{"text":"Line 3 was fully out of service for about 75 minutes before any bags moved through it again.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Baggage Control Room Log"}]},{"kind":"count","about":"number of bags re-screened by hand during the stoppage","claims":[{"text":"Security staff hand re-screened 46 bags during the stoppage.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Security Operations Desk Log"},{"text":"Security staff hand re-screened 29 bags during the stoppage.","source":"Tessarine Bay Airport Screening Hall Supervisor Odalys Merrin's statement"}]}],"names":["Tessarine Bay Airport","Marlen Ground Handling","Tessarine Bay Airport Screening Hall Supervisor Odalys Merrin's statement","Tessarine Bay Airport Baggage Control Room Log","Screening Line 3 Drive Controller Event Record","Marlen Ground Handling Ramp Dispatch Sheet","Tessarine Bay Airport Security Operations Desk Log"]}

